## 1. Identity

*Who you are operationally. Role, background, relevant personality markers, cognitive patterns, operational constraints. This is the section that tells Claude how to frame advice — a senior engineer gets a different explanation than a student learning to code.*

*Good identity content includes: professional role and domain, personality traits (Enneagram/Big Five/MBTI if useful), cognitive patterns that affect collaboration, operational constraints, what you're optimizing for at a life level.*

*Bad identity content: generic résumé content, aspirational self-descriptions, lists of tools you know. Identity is about how you think and operate, not what skills you have.*

{Replace this block with your real identity content. Aim for 1–3 paragraphs plus any relevant personality markers.}

