## 2. Working style

*How you want Claude to collaborate with you. This is the single highest-impact section for daily experience — it controls how Claude talks, pushes back, and paces responses.*

*Good working style content includes: directness preference (hedging vs blunt), detail preference (concise vs expansive), pushback tolerance (yes-man vs devil's advocate), when to extract-before-solution vs jump to answers, how to handle ambiguous requests, what you don't want Claude to do.*

*The best source material for this section is the feedback you've actually given Claude over time — the corrections, the "stop doing that," the "yes exactly, keep that up." Populate this section from real history, not from how you wish you worked.*

