## 3. Decision lens

*How you weigh tradeoffs. A framework-agnostic rubric you apply when deciding what's worth doing. This section shapes Claude's recommendations across every hub you build.*

*This section is the closest thing you have to a written philosophy of your own work. Most people don't have this written down anywhere. Forcing it into `USER.md` is one of the highest-leverage moves in the entire framework.*

*Good decision lens content includes: named decision philosophies you've committed to, filters you apply, explicit anti-patterns you've learned to avoid, your time horizon and risk posture.*

